    "input": {
      "kind": "z80-decode",
      "note": "What readZ80 accepts and rejects (dna/domain/snapshot-z80.md FMT-Z80-VALIDATE-001). Each file is laid out from the documented fields, starting from the pinned FMT-Z80-V3-DECODE-001 header and page blocks: accept cases decode (v3 hardware mode 3 = 48K + M.G.T.; a version-2 file in mode 2 = SamRam; flag byte 12 = 255 read as 1, so border 0 and R bit 7 set; a page block outside the 48K map skipped; two trailing bytes too short for a page header ignored). Reject cases carry expected.error, a case-insensitive pattern the thrown message must match: an empty file; a version-1 image shorter than 48 KB, or compressed and expanding to 16 bytes; a file ending inside the extra header; an extra-header length of 30; 128K hardware modes (4 in version 3, 3 in version 2); a page block running past end-of-file; a page expanding to 16 bytes; a 48K file without page 4 (the pre-2026-11 two-page decode blob); and a 16K snapshot (byte 37 bit 7) that stores only page 8. Before this fixture the reader decoded every one of these into a partly zeroed machine.",
